From 93b1ba425d806358caf1ba99396a9342588a4259 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LegendaryFire <tristan.balon@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:35:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Select the RAM-part pages an Inkling 2 decode reads (opt-in)

A tiered decode read the whole RAM part of every full-attention cache,
so now --kv-select N reads only N tokens of it (Quest page selection):
each page of --kv-page P tokens (default 64) keeps per-channel key
bounds in VRAM, a decode ranks the RAM-part pages by their bound on
q.k (the best of a KV head's query heads, the first page always kept)
and the CPU threads read the best N tokens' worth. The VRAM window and
prompt reading stay exact. Off unless set; needs --kv-resident.

Not exact. 24K text, last 3.8K tokens scored (15-19K RAM-part tokens a
head): nll +0.0015 at P 16 / N 4096 (run-to-run noise), +0.035 at P 64,
+0.10 at P 16 / N 1024. A 58K needle test (three tags at 15/45/75%)
finds all three down to N 1024. Decode at 58K, window 8K: 15.5 -> 31
tok/s. P 16 bounds cost about 1 GiB of VRAM per 512K session.
